<h3>Layer Engagement Patterns</h3>
<p>The paper's analysis of which layers get used reveals a consistent V-shape for 3B models — early and late layers dominate while middle layers are frequently pruned — while 8B models show a smoother decay from early to late, engaging middle layers more consistently. Harder tasks produce more uniform layer usage: on DART-5, even mid-depth layers are activated with comparable frequency to shallow ones, suggesting that complex reasoning needs a broader slice of the model's capacity.</p>

