<p>The key implication: larger models rely less on stereotyped depth patterns. A 3B model tends to always skip the same middle layers regardless of input; an 8B model more intelligently adapts which layers to skip based on what the input actually requires. This distributional flexibility explains the larger CoLa gains on 8B — there's more latent composability to unlock.</p>
</section>

